<title>USA: National-Oilwell Q4 net loss.</title>
<headline>National-Oilwell Q4 net loss.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON, Texas 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter Ended	Year Ended</p>
<p>				December 31,	December 31,</p>
<p>			 1996	     1995     1996	   1995</p>
<p> Revenues	 $180,479	 $145,719 $648,621     $545,803</p>
<p>Operating income</p>
<p>before special</p>
<p>  items	     11,088	    4,118  34,708	  13,781</p>
<p>Net Income (loss)</p>
<p>		  (8,511)(a)	 3,281(b)  245(a)     17,640(b)</p>
<p>Average shares</p>
<p>   outstanding    16,657	    NA(b)  14,357	   NA(b)</p>
<p>Net income</p>
<p>   per share	 (.51)	    NA(b)     .02	   NA(b)</p>
<p>(a) Includes non-recurring special charges of $23,011 ($14,267 after taxes) related to the initial public offering.</p>
<p>(b) Includes non-recurring after tax gain of $1,071 in the fourth quarter and $8,458 for the full year 1995 from the sale of assets.  During 1995, the company operated as a partnership and did not record U.S. income taxes or have outstanding shares of common stock. SOURCE  National-Oilwell, Inc.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
